,0,0).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }i+({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }j+({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(0,0,0) & =({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,i+({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,j+({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186398956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398955 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "91095769-6695-5735-bdf7-d8d4bfdca38b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398956 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4643060a-8d1d-5789-a362-102d70382db9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398957 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\,i+2\\,j+k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398957 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398957 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8070bb66-d16c-505c-85ee-2a417bc81d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398958 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\,i+j+2\\,k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186398958 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/r